cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Project Nira: Open Hardware Microplastics Detector"
message: "If you use this hardware, firmware, or analysis in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "only-foss"
    alias: "only-foss"
    website: "https://github.com/only-foss"
repository-code: "https://github.com/only-foss/Project-Nira"
url: "https://github.com/only-foss/Project-Nira"
abstract: >
  Project Nira is an open-source hardware sensor for detecting microplastics
  in water using capacitance-based differential sensing (FDC1004 + ESP32).
  The v1.5 prototype demonstrates statistically significant separation between
  clean water and microplastic-contaminated water (p < 0.001, shift = 571 ADC units).
keywords:
  - microplastics
  - water quality
  - open hardware
  - capacitance sensing
  - ESP32
  - FDC1004
  - environmental monitoring
  - OSHW
